(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[15 1 "// Finalization (PYS9 (a); doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 218\"): pyi has no reference counts, so an object's"] [16 1 "// death is Go's collector's finding. A tracked object (one with weak references, or with a finalizer's work due: a"] [17 1 "// class's __del__, a generator's close, a socket's warning) has a Go finalizer and a record in tracked, keyed by its"] [18 1 "// address and never holding it. Go's finalizer goroutine only moves the dead object into finQueue and sets the eval"] [19 1 "// breaker's bit; the thread holding the GIL drains the queue (handleEvalBreaker, gc.collect). The order is reference"] [20 1 "// counting's (subtype_dealloc): the work first, the Go finalizer set again without it (PEP 442: once only); found"] [21 1 "// unreachable again, the weak references are cleared (in the Go finalizer, under finMu, so no weak reference yields"] [22 1 "// the object after it) and their callbacks called in CPython's list order. Go's heap does not move and an object with"] [23 1 "// a finalizer is kept until the finalizer ran, so a weak reference's hidden address is valid while it is not cleared."] [25 1 "// the work a tracked object's death runs"] [27 23 "// its class's __del__ (slot_tp_finalize)"] [28 23 "// a generator's, coroutine's or async generator's finalization (_PyGen_Finalize)"] [29 23 "// an open socket's ResourceWarning and close (sock_finalize)"] [30 23 "// an async generator's awaitable never awaited (async_gen_asend_finalize)"] [31 23 "// a built-in type's tp_finalize, the record's fin (TrackFinalizer, queue 241)"] [34 1 "// finTrack is a tracked object's record."] [36 21 "// the object's pointer's element type, to rebuild it from its address"] [37 21 "// its weak references in CPython's order: the basic ref, the basic proxy, then the newest first"] [38 21 "// the work due at its death"] [39 21 "// its identity once hashed (identityHash; an instance keeps it in its own field)"] [40 2 "// aioTask: a registered asyncio task past the strong list (builtins_asyncio.go's registry, queue 224)"] [42 2 "// owner is the interpreter that tracked it (queue 230): its work runs there, nil for the main one before any thread"] [44 2 "// fin is a built-in type's tp_finalize (workFin; queue 241), given the object: it must hold no reference to it"] [48 1 "// finItem is a dead object's turn in the queue: obj and its work, or (obj nil) its weak references' callbacks."] [55 24 "// tracked, finQueue, the weak references' addresses (Go's finalizer goroutine takes it too)"] [58 26 "// the Go finalizers run so far (gc.collect waits until it stays still)"] [59 26 "// a drain is running (under the GIL): a nested one leaves the queue to it"] [61 18 "// PYI_NO_FINALIZERS: nothing tracked (the weak references hold their referents, as before 218)"] [66 1 "// The moment at del (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): DELETE_FAST of a tracked object with work"] [67 1 "// or weak references due asks Go's collector at once whether that was the last reference, and drains the queue before"] [68 1 "// the next instruction: reference counting's moment when it was, a wasted collection when it was not. The collections'"] [69 1 "// time is held to a tenth of the elapsed wall time (and 50 ms); past it the death waits for the next collection."] [75 1 "// finDeletedAt is DELETE_FAST of f's fast local i (not unbound) with the check of the value it deletes. The value is"] [76 1 "// read and cleared here and dropped before anything else runs: no other variable, and no frame of a call goi"] [77 1 "// interprets, keeps it (goi's registers keep a returned call's values: queue 218's REQUEST), so that the collection"] [78 1 "// can find it dead."] [96 1 "// finPeek is the address of the value of name in d, before DELETE_NAME or DELETE_GLOBAL deletes it (0: nothing to"] [97 1 "// check); the deletion's moment is then finDeleted's, as DELETE_FAST's (queue 224: `del g` at a module's level)."] [113 1 "// finDeleted is the check of a deleted object at address a."] [128 1 "// finVerify is the collection at a deletion: rounds while the object's record moves (its work run, then its weak"] [129 1 "// references cleared: subtype_dealloc's two steps), each a Go collection and a wait until the record moved or Go's"] [130 1 "// finalizers are still, then the drain."] [165 1 "// finQueued is whether tr's object is in the queue (finMu held)."] [175 1 "// addrOf is o's address (o a pointer: finTrackable)."] [178 1 "// hiddenPtr reads the address *u as a pointer (a weak reference's referent, alive while not cleared)."] [181 1 "// toObject is the object of type *elem at the address *u (a weak reference's referent; finMu held, *u not 0)."] [186 1 "// finTrackable is o's possible tracking: a pointer to a non-empty type of this package (another package's objects"] [187 1 "// may have their own Go finalizer, which a second SetFinalizer would abort on: _bz2's, _sqlite3's, _zstd's)."] [196 1 "// trackLocked is o's record, made (with its Go finalizer) when o has none; finMu held."] [214 1 "// trackWork tracks o (finTrackable) with the work w due at its death."] [225 1 "// TrackFinalizer is a built-in type's tp_finalize (queue 241): fin(o) runs under the GIL at o's death, once, in"] [226 1 "// __del__'s place in the order (a cycle's too). o is a pointer to a non-empty type with no Go finalizer of its own (a"] [227 1 "// type of another package may be given: pysqlite3's cursor); fin takes o as its argument and must hold no reference"] [228 1 "// to it (the record would keep it alive)."] [245 1 "// goFinalized is the Go finalizer of every tracked object, run on Go's finalizer goroutine: o into the queue."] [271 1 "// drainFinalizers runs the queue under the GIL until it is empty: the number of dead objects handled."] [298 4 "// its interpreter ended: no one to run the work in (queue 230)"] [323 2 "// the record stays (its Go finalizer set again) while weak references, new work or an identity need it"] [336 1 "// runWork runs the work w due at o's death (its record's work already cleared: PEP 442's once)."] [357 1 "// weakCallbacks calls the callbacks of a dead object's weak references, in its list's order (PyObject_ClearWeakRefs)."] [371 1 "// runDel is slot_tp_finalize: the class's __del__ called, its exception to sys.unraisablehook."] [382 1 "// finalizeGen is _PyGen_Finalize: an async generator with sys's finalizer hook handed to it; a coroutine never"] [383 1 "// started warns; a suspended generator or coroutine closed."] [403 1 "// warnUnawaitedCoroutine is _PyErr_WarnUnawaitedCoroutine: warnings._warn_unawaited_coroutine(coro), or a plain"] [404 1 "// RuntimeWarning when that failed other than by the warning itself."] [425 1 "// finUnraisable is PyErr_FormatUnraisable from a finalizer (the object None)."] [432 1 "// finRound is one round of gc.collect: Go's collection, a wait until Go's finalizer goroutine has been still for a"] [433 1 "// moment (there is no public barrier), then the drain; the number of dead objects handled."] [450 1 "// finCollect is gc.collect's finalization: rounds until one handles nothing (at most 8), none when nothing is"] [451 1 "// tracked or queued; then the cycles through finalizers (cyCollect, queue 222) and the rounds again for what their"] [452 1 "// trash held; the number of cyclic trash nodes (CPython's count: acyclic garbage is reference counting's)."] [464 1 "// finRounds is 218's rounds: the dead objects handled."] [467 2 "// the classes' attribute caches out of date are dropped now, not at their next lookup: a stale answer (a method"] [468 2 "// deleted from its class) would keep its value alive"] [492 1 "// finalizeSocket is sock_finalize: an open socket warns ResourceWarning \"unclosed %R\" (its source the socket), then"] [493 1 "// its descriptor is closed."] [510 1 "// resourceWarn is PyErr_ResourceWarning(source, 1, msg): warnings.warn(msg, ResourceWarning, 1, source=source)."] [524 1 "// growStack gives f's value stack room for n more values in a new array, the old one's values cleared: newFrame's one"] [525 1 "// allocation holds the fast locals and the stack's first array together, so the stack's stale values there would keep"] [526 1 "// their objects reachable through the fast locals for the frame's life (queue 218: found by a weak reference that a"] [527 1 "// function's first call did not clear)."] [536 1 "// pendingGens are the coroutines made, and the generators suspended in a try region, since the last flush (under the"] [537 1 "// GIL): one still not finished when the list is flushed (every 256, and in gc.collect) is tracked for its finalization,"] [538 1 "// so the common cases, a coroutine awaited at once and a generator run to its end, pay no Go finalizer (queue 218:"] [539 1 "// measured with bin/pyi aot, a coroutine 0.13 us untracked against 0.6 us tracked at creation; a generator with a"] [540 1 "// try 0.66 us against 1.0-1.2 us tracked at its first suspension)."] [551 1 "// track tracks a generator not finished for its finalization. Its frame's pointer back at it becomes an address: Go"] [552 1 "// never finalizes an object that reaches itself (queue 224: no suspended generator's frame let its generator die, so"] [553 1 "// neither close nor \"never awaited\" ran)."] [563 1 "// generator is f's generator (f.f_generator), nil when none, or when it died first."] [590 1 "// Cycles through finalizers (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): Go never frees a cycle that"] [591 1 "// reaches a finalized object from itself, so gc.collect() finds them as CPython's gc_collect_main does, with Go's"] [592 1 "// collector answering what deduce_unreachable's counts answer: which objects are held from outside. The graph's nodes"] [593 1 "// are instances (their dictionary, while not handed out as an object, and __slots__ folded in), lists, tuples and"] [594 1 "// dictionaries; its edges their slots of interface type that hold a node. Every edge between two probed nodes is"] [595 1 "// hidden (the slot set to nil, its target kept by address), each probed node given a probe's Go finalizer, and Go"] [596 1 "// collects with the GIL held: a node whose probe does not run is held from outside, and so is what it reaches."] [599 27 "// gc.DEBUG_SAVEALL"] [600 27 "// a larger graph is left alone (Go's collection, 218's moment)"] [604 35 "// a probe's answer is being read (finMu): a probe that runs later only holds"] [605 35 "// the probed nodes whose probe ran (finMu), held until the collection ends"] [606 35 "// those that ran after the answer was read"] [607 35 "// tracemalloc traced once: a list, a dict or a cell may carry its Go finalizer"] [608 35 "// gc.set_debug's flags"] [609 35 "// gc.garbage"] [610 2 "// gcCollecting: a gc.collect() runs (gc.collecting: faulthandler's \"Garbage-collecting\" line, queue 241)"] [614 1 "// cyNode is a node of the graph, never holding its object (its address is hidden from the collector)."] [618 18 "// its record when tracked"] [619 18 "// its slots that hold a node, by address: a slot in the node itself (a FutureIter's) must not hold it"] [620 18 "// in step: the slot is a typed pointer (*Dict, *Cell ...), else an Object"] [621 18 "// the nodes they hold, in step"] [628 1 "// cyLeaves are the objects a collection's graph does not walk (queue 241): the dictionaries of the modules sys.modules"] [629 1 "// holds and the builtins' (held from outside: walking them would walk the whole program), and the frames running on a"] [630 1 "// thread's stack (their slots change under the loop; their Go frames hold them). Set by cyCollect, nil otherwise."] [633 1 "// cySetLeaves computes cyLeaves for this collection."] [677 1 "// cyIsNode is whether o is a node: an object whose references cyTraverse lists (CPython's tp_traverse), not a leaf of"] [678 1 "// this collection (cyLeaves), and able to take a probe's Go finalizer (a list's, a dictionary's or a cell's Go finalizer"] [679 1 "// may be tracemalloc's once it traced: then none of them)."] [692 3 "// a frame a Python object may hold (a traceback's, f_back's, gi_frame's), not running on a thread's stack,"] [693 3 "// not of a generator (the generator's slots fold it in: 222's rule)"] [703 1 "// cyWalkable is a generator whose frame's slots can be hidden (queue 224): suspended, with no pointer from its frame"] [704 1 "// back at it (a generator that reaches itself never has a probe run), and its frame not handed out: what else holds"] [705 1 "// an escaped frame is not in the graph."] [710 1 "// cyVisit is cyTraverse's visitor: a slot of the node, its kind (typed: a pointer of a concrete type, else an Object)"] [711 1 "// and the node it holds."] [714 1 "// cyTraverse is tp_traverse (queue 241; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 241\"): f called with each slot of o (a"] [715 1 "// node) that holds a node. Only slots o owns alone are listed: a backing array shared with another holder would hide"] [716 1 "// that holder's reference. A reference the table does not list (a map's, a closure's, a field of a struct that is no"] [717 1 "// object) stays visible to Go's collector, which only keeps more alive."] [785 20 "// handed out as an object: a node of its own (queue 241)"] [792 31 "// _asyncio's Future or Task: the slots of a task's cycle (queue 224)"] [909 1 "// cyGraph is the graph from the seeds (an object a probe would find held stays out of it), nil past cyMaxNodes."] [955 1 "// cyRelevant is the nodes a probe must see: those of a strongly connected component with a cycle and a tracked node"] [956 1 "// (Tarjan's, iterative), and what they reach. An acyclic dead object is Go's to find."] [1049 1 "// cyProbe asks Go's collector which of the nodes in are held from outside the set: the edges between them hidden, a"] [1050 1 "// probe's finalizer on each (a tracked node's own taken off), runtime.GC() with the GIL held, a wait until every"] [1051 1 "// probe ran or Go's finalizers are still; then the slots put back and the probes taken off. The answer: the nodes"] [1052 1 "// reachable (held from outside, or reached from such a node through the edges)."] [1072 2 "// with its probe set each node outlives its last reference: what an earlier probe held is let go now"] [1169 1 "// cyHideRegistries takes the probed nodes out of the runtime's registries that hold their keys where CPython holds"] [1170 1 "// nothing (queue 241, \"Design: 241\": the weak registries): id()'s identities of untracked objects and the functions'"] [1171 1 "// annotations. The returned function puts back the reachable nodes' entries once the answer is read; the trash's go"] [1172 1 "// (a tracked node's identity into its record), so that Go can free it."] [1206 22 "// the trash's identity in its record, should a finalizer resurrect it"] [1217 1 "// cyDebug (PYI_GC_DEBUG=1): each probe prints to stderr its nodes held from outside that no other probed node holds,"] [1218 1 "// the roots of what it keeps (queue 241: what to look at when a cycle is not found)."] [1253 1 "// cySetFinalizer gives n's object the probe's Go finalizer (a tracked node's own taken off first: Go allows one)."] [1262 1 "// cyRestore gives a surviving tracked node its own Go finalizer again (its record dropped when it needs none)."] [1279 1 "// cyClearWeakRefs clears the weak references to the trash's tracked nodes (handle_weakrefs): their callbacks, in each"] [1280 1 "// list's order, returned to be called once all are cleared (a weak reference is never a node: always \"outside\")."] [1300 1 "// cyCollect is gc.collect()'s cycle detection: the trash found, PEP 442's order run over it; the number of trash nodes."] [1362 1 "// cyCount is the probed nodes whose probe ran (finMu held)."] [1382 1 "// cyFind is the cyclic trash: from the tracked nodes (or, only given, from those nodes alone: the resurrection's"] [1383 1 "// check), the graph, its relevant part probed; every probed node restored but the trash's (they keep no Go finalizer)."] [1406 1 "// cySeedGraph builds the graph and its relevant part in a frame of its own, so no object of the walk stays in a live"] [1407 1 "// variable of the probe's caller."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[87 28] [107 28] [135 16] [135 27] [140 29] [140 56] [148 29] [198 21] [205 27] [249 21] [296 16] [345 29] [365 51] [377 42] [389 55] [398 24] [407 39] [408 64] [419 92] [427 25] [438 28] [438 55] [440 28] [476 16] [476 27] [499 51] [504 16] [571 21] [654 33] [667 19] [667 29] [720 13] [730 13] [735 13] [740 13] [745 13] [750 13] [755 13] [760 13] [765 13] [792 17] [817 26] [890 18] [916 21] [920 23] [933 12] [933 28] [939 18] [968 22] [968 39] [996 32] [1101 52] [1110 27] [1110 54] [1118 27] [1189 28] [1193 28] [1194 30] [1203 22] [1318 34] [1339 41] [1366 30] [1420 33]]} (go/file "finalize.go" :imports [


